  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 77be8d3abc4d614408c62dfb3862c314, type: 3}
  m_Name: J1_Seq05_1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SpeakerTextSO
  showScore: 0
  dialogues:
  - character: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c8fcfa5882242b84b8bf1fb55659059e, type: 2}
    emotion: 0
    text: 'Now the project is on site your main role is to track any changes to the
      design, and ensure your subcontractors are sent instructions for any new work
      that arises, and paid for those instructions.

'
  - character: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c8fcfa5882242b84b8bf1fb55659059e, type: 2}
    emotion: 0
    text: The old building has been demolished, your ground work has been laid, the
      new building has been built and all plumbing/electrical/carpentry has been
      installed. It is time to complete the flooring.
  - character: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c8fcfa5882242b84b8bf1fb55659059e, type: 2}
    emotion: 0
    text: You discover that the screed installer has installed the screed too low
      which means that the floor levels are incorrect.
  - character: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c8fcfa5882242b84b8bf1fb55659059e, type: 2}
    emotion: 0
    text: The screeder has been paid and while they have a few men left on site doing
      final touches, they refuse to fix the level saying they were told by the site
      team the level to screed to.
